# GRAMSEVAMITRA CURSOR RULES

## Tech Stack Constraints
- Framework: React / Astro / Tailwind CSS
- Native Mobile Shell: Capacitor (Android focus)
- Document Engine: @capacitor-mlkit/document-scanner
- Image Engine: HTML5 Canvas API + @capacitor-community/image-manipulator + @capawesome/capacitor-photo-manipulator
- Video Engine: @whiteguru/capacitor-plugin-video-editor
- Local Storage: IndexedDB / OPFS (PWA) + Capacitor Filesystem (Mobile Native)
- NO external UI component libraries unless explicitly specified.
- NEVER suggest switching frameworks or adding heavy cloud dependencies.

## Platform Isolation Rules
- NEVER use the same UI component for desktop and mobile without a `usePlatform()` guard.
- Desktop PWA components must live in `src/desktop/`.
- Mobile Capacitor components must live in `src/mobile/`.
- Shared business logic (API calls, storage, utilities) lives in `src/shared/`.
- If a file imports a mobile-specific component into a desktop view, flag it as a violation.

## Plugin & Android Safety Rules
- ONLY use official `@capacitor/*` or highly maintained `@capawesome/*` plugins. Do NOT install unmaintained `@capacitor-community` plugins without explicit user approval.
- If an image/video manipulation task can be done securely via HTML5 Canvas API instead of a native plugin, default to Canvas to prevent build errors.
- Always check and update `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` when adding plugins that require permissions (Camera, Read/Write External Storage, Internet).

## Anti-Hallucination & Execution Rules
1. Atomic Changes Only: Modify or create at most 2–3 files per task. Never refactor untouched files.
2. Type Safety First: Define or update TypeScript interfaces/types BEFORE writing logic.
3. No Unused Code: Do not leave placeholder comments, mock functions, or dead code.
4. Environment Awareness: Always use `Capacitor.isNativePlatform()` to isolate native mobile features from PWA desktop features.
5. GitHub Workflow: Every complete atomic task MUST end with a git commit and push instruction.

## File Size & Bundle Rules
- Never bundle a file >50KB in the initial payload. Use dynamic imports for heavy modules.
- The initial app shell must load in <2 seconds on a 4G connection.

## Commit Rules
- Every commit must have a `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, or `chore:` prefix.
- Never commit without running `npm run build` first to check for errors.
